IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `il37-nouns`
IMPORT `il37-seat`

-- Tests for the seat layer: the questions of a candidate and of a judge give the answers of the rules they call. Row IL-37.
-- Expected values are worked from the text (s 4(d), (e), (f); s 7(4)); the inputs of the first question are in the order: the court is the Supreme Court, the coalition has more than 80,
-- President, justice, justice, Minister of Justice, other minister, coalition Knesset member, opposition Knesset member, first public representative, second public representative.

§ `Was the committee's choice of me valid?`

-- A district court: five, one from each paragraph, a judge among them (President, Minister of Justice, coalition Knesset member, opposition Knesset member, justice).
#ASSERT `was the committee's choice of me valid on the votes it got` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- The same five with the opposition Knesset member against and the opposition's public representative for: the representative stands for paragraph (3).
#ASSERT `was the committee's choice of me valid on the votes it got` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Five without a judge: not valid for a district court, valid for the Supreme Court (s 4(e)).
#ASSERT `was the committee's choice of me valid on the votes it got` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `was the committee's choice of me valid on the votes it got` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- More than 80 coalition Knesset members: the opposition Knesset member's consent is not needed, and two of the ministers and the coalition Knesset member are.
#ASSERT `was the committee's choice of me valid on the votes it got` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `was the committee's choice of me valid on the votes it got` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Can the committee end my term?`

#ASSERT `can the committee end my term on the votes it got` `the Minister of Justice, as chair of the committee` `the text from the 26th Knesset` 9 7 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `can the committee end my term on the votes it got` `the Minister of Justice, as chair of the committee` `the text from the 26th Knesset` 9 6 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `can the committee end my term on the votes it got` `someone else` `the text from the 26th Knesset` 9 9 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `can the committee end my term on the votes it got` `the Commissioner for Complaints against Judges` `the text before the 26th Knesset` 7 7 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `can the committee end my term on the votes it got` `the Commissioner for Complaints against Judges` `the transitional window of Amendment No. 4 section 3` 9 8 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `can the committee end my term on the votes it got` `the Commissioner for Complaints against Judges` `the transitional window of Amendment No. 4 section 3` 9 9 EQUALS TRUE
